mfg/part-map.csv:4:joystick-nub,CAP1,"Joystick cap CAP1, round, with its 6.90 x 6.40 flange (one moulded part; design v7, folder name kept)"
mfg/parts-notes.md:26:- **joystick-cap** (STEP and STL): CAP1, the round cap: shank dia 4.40 with its rounded top edge, spherical dish and three ridges, and its 6.90 x 6.40 x 0.40 flange; one moulded part, written as two touching solids (shank and flange, 78.7324 mm3 together). Placed at the US 9 position (-78 deg); the same part at every size (the shank from the flange top to the rim plane is 4.110 to 4.118 mm in the seven size builds, within the model's 0.01 surface probe step; export logs, line "joystick US"). Spec: `specs/joystick-nub.md`.
mfg/parts-notes.md:27:- **joystick-frame** (STEP and STL): FRM1, the round frame ring, outer dia 5.40, bore 4.80, 1.30 long; placed at the US 9 position. Spec: `specs/joystick-nub.md`.
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:63:| Joystick frame | FRM1 | round titanium ring, 5.40 outer diameter, 4.80 bore, 1.30 long, coated gloss black with the body, bonded in the round 5.60 opening with DP420 Black | `design/architecture.md:826`, `design/bom.csv:82`, `design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:1` | 13 |
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:185:- **Join:** first the frame FRM1 (titanium grade 5, 5.40 outer diameter, 4.80 bore, 1.30 long, coated gloss black in the same batch as the body) is bonded into the round 5.60 opening from outside the band with 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black epoxy, 0.10 mm radial gap filled all round (`design/bom.csv:82`, `design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:23`). Cure: 24 h at 22 C with no heat, the room temperature cure of 3M's data sheet for DP420 Black (revision June 2024, page 3: 4,500 psi overlap shear on aluminium after 24 h at 22 C); no oven, because the membranes of step 11 and the gaskets of step 12 are already in the body. Then the round cap CAP1 (`joystick_cap`, Makrolon 2407 colour 901510, shank 4.40 and flange as one moulded part, `design/bom.csv:81`) goes in straight from the bore: the 6.90 x 6.40 flange rises through the 7.0 x 6.8 pocket (0.05 mm on each side along the finger, 0.2 mm round the band), the 4.40 shank passes up through the 4.80 bore of FRM1 with 0.20 mm radial clearance, and the flange stops under the pocket roof, 0.05 mm below it, held on all four sides by the roof round the 5.60 opening (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:249`, `design/architecture.md:826`).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:187:- **Before:** steps 10 to 12 passed. FRM1 and the body were coated in the same batch (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:22`). The bonding faces are degreased with isopropyl alcohol [PROPOSED: reason, the coated faces carry handling oil]. The DP420 has cured 24 h at 22 C before CAP1 goes in, because the cap is centred by the frame's bore and the frame must not move. The harness is not yet in the channel: the cap must go in before the switch head, which lies under the flange on the bore side (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:255`).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:338:| 2 | Joystick: the frame FRM1 seam and the cap CAP1 in its bore | the frame seam is closed by the DP420 Black bond all round (step 13); the cap has 0.20 mm radial clearance in the bore and no seal (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:48`); sealing at the cap is a bench question (B9, `design/architecture.md:511`). The switches themselves are rated "IP6X and IPX7" (`design/architecture.md:47`) | the pocket behind the cap may get wet only if nothing is harmed: switches sealed, their joints inside the cast resin, the dam DAM1 tight (`design/bom.csv:55`; edge only, K15) | needs a test (and a dam material, S26, and an answer to K-A12) |
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:367:| Adhesive of the joystick frame: fixed, 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black, 24 h at 22 C | 13 | fixed in v7 (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:23`); bench B9 proves the bond on the coated titanium | B9 |
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:369:| Cap CAP1 and frame FRM1: fixed, Makrolon 2407 colour 901510 moulded; Ti-6Al-4V turned, separate part | 13 | fixed in v7 (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:16`); a moulder and the body maker quote (`design/bom.csv:81`, `design/bom.csv:82`) | B9 |
mfg/mfg-notes.md:13:- What draw.py cannot do: dimension an inside feature on the views. It draws the outline with hidden edges dashed and dimensions only the overall size; the pockets, slots, roof and the motor window are given in each body sheet's table (values from the model), the cap and frame dimensions in `specs/joystick-nub.md`.
